{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "label": "Design decisions", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_bunfirst", "label": "Why Bun first", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fast cold start, built-in SQLite / test runner / HTTP, and modern runtime ergonomics. The framework stays runtime-agnostic \u2014 Node is fully supported, Deno best-effort \u2014 Bun is only the primary target for testing and benchmarks."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_tspattern", "label": "Why ts-pattern (not switch or if/else)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compile-time exhaustiveness so a new variant cannot silently fall through, type narrowing inside arms without casts, and a scannable dispatch table because every arm is a one-line delegation to an onXxx handler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_singlethreadedmodel", "label": "Why a single-threaded model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JavaScript is single-threaded per process and both alternatives cost more than they return, so parallelism comes from clustering across processes or a worker mesh \u2014 neither of which reintroduces the shared-mutable-state problems of multi-threaded JVM actor systems."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_crdtselection", "label": "Why these CRDTs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counters, sets, registers and maps cover the common 95 % of distributed-state use cases. Sequence and tree CRDTs are niche, hard to get right and better served by domain-specific libraries."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_nostreamsdsl", "label": "Why no Streams DSL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Porting a backpressure/materializer/graph-DSL streams library to TypeScript would be a major project on its own; the framework scope is the actor model, clustering and persistence."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_hoconconfig", "label": "Why HOCON instead of YAML or TOML", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is the de-facto JVM config format, so readers land in a familiar shape, and it brings env substitution, duration and size types, and object merging that YAML and TOML lack."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_hoconnoinclude", "label": "HOCON include directives are refused", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Honouring an include would let whoever writes a config source pick which further files and URLs the process reads; compose the sources in code instead."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_explicitreplyto", "label": "Why explicit replyTo refs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An implicit sender works for opt-in replies, but an explicit replyTo is type-safe \u2014 the message type declares what reply to expect and the compiler can verify it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_nocrossactortransactions", "label": "Why no cross-actor transactions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Distributed transaction protocols are complex and brittle in real networks; sagas with explicit compensation are easier to reason about and match actor semantics better, so the cost-benefit of built-in transactions is not there."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_architecture_decision_records_noadrlog", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_bunfirst", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_tspattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_singlethreadedmodel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_crdtselection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_nostreamsdsl", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_hoconconfig", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_explicitreplyto", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/design-decisions.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_designdecisions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_extras_design_decisions_nocrossactortransactions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/extras/desig